{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-129031",
  "enisaUuid": "30471405-1283-3e7f-bedf-834f0706361d",
  "description": "A vulnerability in the debug logging functionality of ClamAV could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause a DoS condition on an affected device.\r\n\r This vulnerability is due to improper handling of logging values. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by submitting a file to be scanned by the software that has debug logging enabled. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the ClamAV scanning process to terminate, resulting in a DoS condition on the affected software.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 18, 2026, 4:32:32 PM",
